From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: bugfix/round-video-muted-gif: a converted video message without sound must not become a GIF

SendMessagesHelper.prepareSendingVideo adds TL_documentAttributeAnimated to every muted
video it converts, video messages included: a trimmed camera video message recorded or
previewed without sound, or a silent gallery video sent as a video message, then goes
out with both round_message and the GIF attribute and is shown as an animation. Muted
video messages now take the regular branch (duration from the edited info, size from the
crop), like unmuted ones; muted regular videos still become GIFs as before.
---
 TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/SendMessagesHelper.java | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/SendMessagesHelper.java b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/SendMessagesHelper.java
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/SendMessagesHelper.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/SendMessagesHelper.java
@@ -12211,7 +12211,7 @@ public class SendMessagesHelper extends BaseController implements NotificationCe
                         attributeVideo.duration = videoEditedInfo.estimatedDuration / 1000.0;
                         document.size = videoEditedInfo.estimatedSize;
                     } else if (videoEditedInfo != null && videoEditedInfo.needConvert()) {
-                        if (videoEditedInfo.muted) {
+                        if (videoEditedInfo.muted && !isRound) {
                             document.attributes.add(new TLRPC.TL_documentAttributeAnimated());
                             fillVideoAttribute(videoPath, attributeVideo, videoEditedInfo);
                             videoEditedInfo.originalWidth = attributeVideo.w;
